{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"J1 acb2 PUSHED FOR REVIEW.\nPre-flight all green: make lint (ruff+zizmor+actionlint), make typecheck (mypy 381 files), make test = 7471 passed / 37 skipped / 114 deselected / 0 FAILED in 28m10s. (The background wrapper reported exit -1, but that was the detached wrapper — pytest itself completed and passed; verified in the captured output.)\nCommit 7fc96b277, trailers verified: rebar-ticket: acb2-1823-2f0d-415b + Change-Id + Signed-off-by RebarBotNava <joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com>. rebar verify-commit-ticket --rev HEAD -> OK.\nGERRIT HICCUP + FIX: the first push (change 1008) drew Gerrit warnings for the 50/72 commit-message rule (subject 66 chars, many body lines >72) — this repo ENFORCES that rule (commit 514d), so I amended: subject now 42 chars, zero lines >72. The amend regenerated the Change-Id, so the re-push created change 1009 and orphaned 1008; ABANDONED 1008 via the REST API with a note pointing at 1009. Lesson for the rest of the stack: write commit messages to 50/72 BEFORE the first push, since amending after a push can rotate the Change-Id.\nCHANGE UNDER REVIEW: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1009 — awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785337014959869001,"uuid":"72d8c122-9775-480a-b068-4334305689d5"}